2026-10-08|Remove Outermost Parentheses

Question
Given a valid parentheses string `s`, remove the outermost parentheses from every primitive part of its decomposition and return the resulting string.

Approach
1. Maintain a `balance` variable.

2. Traverse the string character by character.

3. For `(`:
   - If `balance > 0`, this `(` is not the outermost opening parenthesis, so add it to the answer.
   - Then increase `balance`.

4. For `)`:
   - First decrease `balance`.
   - If `balance > 0` after decreasing, this `)` is not the outermost closing parenthesis, so add it to the answer.

5. When `balance` becomes `0`, we have finished one primitive substring.

6. The first `(` and final `)` of every primitive are therefore automatically skipped.

7. Time complexity is O(n), where n is the length of the string.

8. Space complexity is O(n) for the resulting string.

Solution
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

string removeOuterParentheses(string s) {
    string ans;
    int balance = 0;

    for (char ch : s) {
        if (ch == '(') {
            if (balance > 0) {
                ans.push_back(ch);
            }

            balance++;
        }
        else {
            balance--;

            if (balance > 0) {
                ans.push_back(ch);
            }
        }
    }

    return ans;
}

int main() {
    string s;
    cin >> s;

    cout << removeOuterParentheses(s) << endl;

    return 0;
}
